      <metadata>
        <description><![CDATA[{\rtf1\ansi\deff0{\fonttbl{\f0 \fswiss Helvetica;}{\f1 \fmodern Courier;}}
{\colortbl;\red255\green0\blue0;\red0\green0\blue255;}
\widowctrl\hyphauto

{\pard \ql \f0 \fs24 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 \outlinelevel0 \b \fs34 AutoColor\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \fs24 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 Colour tracks, items, regions and markers from their {\b names}, using plain substring, glob, or {\b real regular expressions}.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \fs24 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 One ordered rule list per object kind -- Tracks, Items, Regions, Markers -- and within a kind the first rule that matches wins, so precedence works like firewall rules. Reordering track rules can never change which region wins.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \fs24 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 The configuration window needs ReaImGui 0.10+. Every other action, including Apply and Clear, works without it.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \fs24 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 MIT licensed. Source: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://github.com/michal-bartak/AutoColor"}}{\fldrslt{\ul
https://github.com/michal-bartak/AutoColor
}}}
\par}
}
]]></description>
